From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:01:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost/kbase: import dma-bufs inner-shareable

Imported dma-bufs were mapped outer-shareable (BASE_MEM_COHERENT_SYSTEM).
The same buffers are mapped inner-shareable by the vendor driver in other
GPU clients (SurfaceFlinger, the app's compositor), so the GPU saw one
physical page with conflicting shareability: intermittent
GPU_SHAREABILITY_FAULT (0x88) and a full GPU reset on MT6897 (Mali-G615).
Use BASE_MEM_COHERENT_LOCAL, as the DDK does.

Tested: PanProbe 38/38 x3; Hades faults 8/8 launches before, 0/7 after;
Moonlighter 5/5 before, 0/6 after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR
(cherry picked from commit f852462fd80fb625f45eaa9ebd84d319dae6837e)

Purpose: fix intermittent GPU_SHAREABILITY_FAULT + GPU reset when importing dma-bufs shared with vendor-driver clients
Upstream-commit: none (kbase backend only)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: kbase-common/files (kbase_kmod.c), csf-v11/110
Validation test: PanProbe 38/38 x3; Hades 0/7 launches faulting (8/8 before); Moonlighter 0/6 (5/5 before)
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
index 36caa970..1741dc0e 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -2013,10 +2013,17 @@ kbase_kmod_import_dmabuf(struct pan_kmod_dev *dev,
       goto err_free_bo;
    }
 
+   /* Import dma-bufs inner-shareable (COHERENT_LOCAL), like the vendor DDK.
+    * The same buffers are mapped by other GPU clients (SurfaceFlinger, the
+    * app's compositor) through the vendor driver with inner shareability;
+    * mapping them outer-shareable (COHERENT_SYSTEM) here makes the GPU see one
+    * physical page with conflicting shareability, which raises an
+    * intermittent GPU_SHAREABILITY_FAULT (0x88) and a full GPU reset on
+    * MT6897 (ACE-Lite). */
    uint64_t import_flags =
       BASE_MEM_PROT_CPU_RD | BASE_MEM_PROT_CPU_WR |
       BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_RD | BASE_MEM_PROT_GPU_WR |
-      BASE_MEM_IMPORT_SHARED | BASE_MEM_COHERENT_SYSTEM;
+      BASE_MEM_IMPORT_SHARED | BASE_MEM_COHERENT_LOCAL;
 
    if (kmod_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_GPU_UNCACHED)
       import_flags |= BASE_MEM_UNCACHED_GPU;
